REGIONAL REGULATION OF EAST LUWU REGENCY

NUMBER 4 OF 2021

CONCERNING

PROTECTION OF WOMEN AGAINST VIOLENCE

BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD

THE REGENT OF EAST LUWU,

Considering : a. that in order to fulfill the constitutional rights of women to be free from torture and treatment that degrades human dignity and to improve the quality of life of women who are entitled to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of violence;

b. that Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence, provides affirmation of the need for protection and provision of a sense of security to women;

c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letters a and b, it is necessary to establish a

Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women

Against Violence;

In view of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;

2. Law Number 39 of 1999 concerning Human Rights (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia

Year 1999 Number 165, Supplement to the State Gazette of

the Republic of Indonesia Number 3886);

3. Law Number 7 of 2003 concerning the Establishment of East Luwu Regency and North

Mamuju Regency in South Sulawesi Province (State

Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2003 Number 27, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number

4. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence

(State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004

Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the

Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);

5. Law Number 44 of 2008 concerning Pornography (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2008 Number 181, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4928);

6. Law Number 16 of 2011 concerning Legal Aid (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2011 Number 104, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5248);

7. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as amended several times most recently by Law

Number 11 of 2020 concerning Job Creation (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2020 Number 245, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 6573);

8. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for the Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4604);

9. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 2 of 2008 concerning Guidelines for the Implementation of Protection of Women;

10. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 1 of 2010 concerning Minimum Service Standards for Integrated Services for Women and Children Victims of Violence (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2010 Number 56);

11. Regulation of the Minister of Home Affairs Number 12 of 2017 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment and Classification of Branch Offices and Regional Technical Implementation Units (State News of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2017 Number 451);

12. Regulation of the State Minister for Women's Empowerment Number 4 of 2018 concerning Guidelines for the Establishment of Regional Technical Implementation Units for the Protection of Women and Children (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2018 Number 532);

13. Regional Regulation of East Luwu Regency Number 8 of 2016 concerning the Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus (Regional Gazette of East Luwu Regency Year 2016 Number 8) as amended by Regional Regulation of East Luwu Regency Number 5 of 2020 concerning Amendment to Regional Regulation of East Luwu Regency Number 8 of 2016 concerning the Establishment and Composition of Regional Apparatus (Regional Gazette of East Luwu Regency Year 2020 Number 5, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of East Luwu Regency Number 124).

With the Joint Approval of

THE REGIONAL HOUSE OF REPRESENTATIVES

and

THE REGENT OF EAST LUWU

HAS DECIDED:

To establish : REGIONAL REGULATION CONCERNING PROTECTION OF WOMEN AGAINST VIOLENCE.

Article 7

(1) In the protection of women, violence prevention is carried out. (2) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) is implemented by: a. socializing laws and regulations;

b. providing education on the dangers of violence against women; c. conducting seminars/workshops or similar activities;

d. establishing cooperation with government agencies or non-government institutions in violence prevention efforts; and

e. establishing a prevention system, mapping locations or areas prone to violence.

(3) Violence prevention as referred to in paragraph (2) may coordinate with other institutions.

Article 13

(1) Assistance Services as referred to in Article 9 letter b, are provided in each type of health service, rehabilitation, legal aid, social reintegration, and repatriation.

(2) Assistance is provided by experts who have expertise in conducting counseling, therapy and/or advocacy for the empowerment and recovery of women victims of violence.

(3) Experts who provide assistance as referred to in paragraph (2) cooperate with UPTD PPA.

(4) Experts as referred to in paragraph (2) must be provided by the Regional Apparatus responsible for women.

(5) Experts as referred to in paragraph (2) consist of: a. health workers;

b. advocates;

c. social workers;

d. spiritual counselors; and

e. psychologists or psychiatrists.

Article 4

Women victims of violence have the right to:

a. have their dignity and honor respected as human beings;
b. obtain information on the protection of women;
c. obtain social rehabilitation and reintegration;
d. obtain physical, psychological and sexual health recovery according to the suffering experienced by victims of violence;
e. obtain empowerment and legal assistance; and f. spiritual guidance services.

Article 21

(1) In order to achieve the objectives of protecting women from acts of violence, the Regional Government may cooperate with: a. Ministries;

b. Provincial Regional Government;

c. Regency/City Regional Government;

d. Universities; and

e. Non-governmental institutions.

(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. exchange of data and information;

b. rehabilitation of victims of violence;

c. repatriation and social reintegration; and

d. provision of evidence and witnesses.

Article 9

Types of services for victims of violence include:

a. complaint and consultation services;
b. assistance services;
c. legal aid services;
d. health services;
e. social rehabilitation services;
f. repatriation services; and
g. social reintegration services.

Article 8

Services for victims of violence are implemented based on the principles of: a. no fees charged;

b. fast;

c. safe and comfortable;

d. empathy;

e. non-judgmental;

f. non-discriminatory; and

g. guaranteed confidentiality.

